      title: 'session VAL 하향 이탈 뒤 빠른 내부 종가에 long·sweep low stop', originalTitle: 'Most traders wait for a liquidity sweep, then a market structure shift. But that’s usually where price stalls, chops, and stops you out. Here’s the real difference: Most of the time, price is trading inside a high-volume range. That’s where buyers and sellers agree on price. That’s fair value. The edge isn’t inside the range. The edge is outside of it. Wait for price to push below the value area, then quickly close back inside. That close is your long entry. Stop goes at the low. Simple. Clean. Repeatable.',
